(PASSIVE ABILITIES) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Every species has at least one passive ability that fires on its own: summoning) Tj
T*
(weather on entry, healing a little each turn, raising defence when struck,) Tj
T*
(shrugging off status, or boosting one type of move. Abilities are what turn a) Tj
T*
(battle from rock-paper-scissors into a puzzle, and the game announces each one) Tj
T*
(the moment it triggers, so a player learns them by watching.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(THE SIGNATURE IDEA: LINEAGE) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Most games in this genre give you a random colour variant you cannot influence.) Tj
T*
(Ours is different, and it is the heart of the design.) Tj
T*
T*
(Every creature carries a permanent, visible record of where it came from and) Tj
T*
(what it inherited. That record has three parts:) Tj
T*
T*
(- Heritage traits, which pass down and affect battle. Breeding combines the) Tj
T*
(  parents' traits under clear rules, so chaining generations produces) Tj
T*
(  combinations that do not exist in the wild.) Tj
T*
(- Marks - visible patterns and colours that show ancestry. Because Marks are) Tj
T*
(  heritable, you can breed toward the look you want instead of hoping for it.) Tj
T*
(  That turns a lottery into a project.) Tj
T*
(- Origin - the wild area it came from, or the player whose line it descends) Tj
T*
(  from, shown as a small family tree on the creature's card.) Tj
T*
T*
(This changes what trading means. You are not swapping a stat block; you are) Tj
T*
(swapping a history. It also gives the game an engine for endless variety at no) Tj
T*
(art cost, which is the one place a small team can genuinely out-produce a large) Tj
T*
(one.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
