/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Two settings: Easy and Standard. Easy softens damage, is more forgiving on) Tj
T*
(accuracy, avoids early difficulty spikes and lets you retry a lost battle.) Tj
T*
(Standard is the intended experience and is a real game, not a walkover.) Tj
T*
T*
(The tone is an adventure with genuine twists and turns, carried with humour -) Tj
T*
(real stakes and real surprises, never grim.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(SAVES) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(Three save slots, each a separate game with its own trainer, playtime, badges) Tj
T*
(and collection. Progress saves automatically when you change area and after) Tj
T*
(battles. Saves are versioned so an update never wipes progress, and a save can) Tj
T*
(be exported as a code to move between devices.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(THE SHAPE OF THE STORY) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(A young trainer leaves a coastal village, chooses a first creature, and sets) Tj
T*
(out to earn four badges across Rivenmoor. A rival appears at milestones, always) Tj
T*
(a step ahead. An outfit is working a plan of its own that runs underneath the) Tj
T*
(badge hunt and only becomes clear later. The chapter ends at the league tower,) Tj
T*
(with the immediate story resolved and larger questions deliberately left open.) Tj
T*
T*
